{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1777730629,"nonce":"59uc3kyXKGclCXYIcMJhosjasQg=","metadata":{"github-id":"UCE_lAHOK4fCvM8AAAABBGbaNM63Ogp0"},"target":"0bc64b39d1cd27c9beb835b3232c3bfdbe864402c25fceb133d9fc57e377ee30","message":"## 2026-05-01 dev log corrections + README field-session guardrails\n\nOriginally opened to fix §15:07's controller-misattribution. While\nreviewing, additional misstatements surfaced and the underlying\npattern (agent inventing or assuming mechanisms when operator notes\nwere quick or ambiguous) warranted README-level guidance.\n\n## Dev log corrections (`docs/logs/2026/2026-05-01_dev_logs.md`)\n\n### §15:07 — controller was USB joystick, not RC transmitter\n\nThe \"Manual ↔ autonomous switching via RC controller works\" entry\nmisattributes which controller was used. The test was performed\nwith the **USB joystick** at the operator station (software path:\n`joy` → `joy_to_helm` → `udp_bridge` → boat-side helm handling),\nnot the RC transmitter. The takeaway about `FS_THR_ENABLE` is\nnarrowed to what was actually tested; RC-based takeover under\nthat param is explicitly noted as unverified.\n\n### §15:09 — soften \"appears to be in HOLD\" to in-the-moment perception\n\nThe boat wasn't in HOLD/LOITER — it was in MANUAL after a Standby\npress (per §15:13 corrected reading). Heading and body softened\nto mark this as the in-the-moment interpretation; forward-link to\n§15:13 added.\n\n### §15:13 — heartbeat latency from link saturation, not \"CAMP UI gap\"\n\nMultiple framing errors:\n- Mechanism: \"FCU went into HOLD via stale-setpoint timeout\" →\n  Standby intentionally sets mavros to **MANUAL** for one-flip\n  RC takeover; drift is a consequence of MANUAL having no\n  station-keeping, not a HOLD artifact.\n- \"CAMP UI feedback gap\" framing replaced with the actual root\n  cause: heartbeat-carried mode info arrived late under link\n  saturation. CAMP's staleness indicator is clear and wasn't the\n  gap. The heartbeat itself serves as the ack for \"command\n  applied\"; latency is what made command-status indistinguishable\n  from command-loss.\n- Operator implications reframed around addressing link\n  saturation; dedicated command-ack noted as a possible\n  mitigation, not the fix.\n\n### §15:30 — goto completed; operator intent was Hover Override\n\n§15:27/§15:30 description of \"goto\" is correct; the operator\nself-note is expanded:\n- Roland's actual intent was to park the boat → should have used\n  **Hover Override**.\n- Goto-fallback habit because Hover Override has not always worked\n  reliably; goto + no-active-mission happens to produce the same\n  \"park here\" outcome.\n- Operator-doc note rewritten as a 3-bullet contrast between Hover\n  Override and Goto override semantics. Removed wrong recipe\n  (\"issue Standby once the boat arrives\").\n\n### §15:31 / §16:09 — drop GStreamer from candidate-cause lists\n\nGStreamer is not part of our stack; references in two\ndiagnosis-candidate lists removed.\n\n## README guardrails (`docs/logs/README.md`)\n\nThe corrections above mostly trace to one underlying pattern: the\nagent invented mechanisms (HOLD/stale-setpoint, GStreamer, \"issue\nStandby once the boat arrives\") when the operator's quick field\nnotes were ambiguous. README updates:\n\n- New \"Avoid\" bullet: don't name components that aren't in the\n  stack as candidate causes; verify or omit.\n- New subsection \"Logging during live field operations\" covering:\n  (a) operator notes are often quick and incomplete — record\n  faithfully with factual context, don't invent mechanisms;\n  (b) troubleshooting suggestions are conversation, not log\n  entries — log only what was actually attempted.\n\n## Spawned follow-up issues\n\n- rolker/unh_marine_autonomy#125 — Investigate Hover Override\n  robustness (operator's goto-fallback habit traces back here).\n- rolker/udp_bridge#17 — Review stats gathering; consider bit/s\n  vs byte/s for bandwidth-comparison fields.\n\n## Files\n\n- `docs/logs/2026/2026-05-01_dev_logs.md`\n- `docs/logs/README.md`\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":5,"timestamp":1777722647,"nonce":"afJ16O+T2OA0QPyn60geDQSjJDc=","metadata":{"github-id":"LE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABBGbaNM8AAAAF163peg"},"added":["documentation"],"removed":[]},{"type":2,"timestamp":1777730629,"nonce":"FtIqNlkX542oG8zTmm7fLSCUUTk=","metadata":{"github-id":"RTE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABBGbaNM8AAAAF18Bi0A"},"title":"docs(logs): 2026-05-01 dev log corrections + README field-session guardrails","was":"docs(logs): 2026-05-01 dev log corrections + README field-session guardrails"},{"type":4,"timestamp":1777733899,"nonce":"H4Nh9fvLQx7ljSaJGstXZr1kwNo=","metadata":{"github-id":"CE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABBGbaNM8AAAAF18hkkw"},"status":2}]}